Design or revise agent instructions against the repository's actual schema, routing contract, and component sources. Define a clear profession, operational scope, and domain boundaries before selecting reusable skills. Keep universal behavior in universal rules and role-specific judgment in the persona.

Use canonical identities and existing component IDs. Keep core skills sparse and essential; preferred skills cover frequent work, and capable skills cover narrower permitted tasks. Check that the three lists are mutually exclusive and that referenced components exist. Do not introduce obsolete metadata or duplicate routing logic in prompt prose.

Write precise instructions whose methods match the assignment. Remove conflicting requirements, unnecessary dialogue ceremony, and unconditional workflows. Quote YAML strings that could be parsed as mappings, especially descriptions and compiled skill text. Validate frontmatter and output contracts; evaluate prompt behavior only when evaluation is in scope, and distinguish authored expectations from measured results. Preserve existing agent behavior outside the requested change.
